The adapted contract includes the seven-joint reset pose and noise, robot base
pose, T workpiece dimensions/mass/friction, spawn distribution, fixed goal,
100-step horizon, state observation fields, dense reward, 64x64 pseudo-render
coverage calculation, and 90 percent success threshold. AVBD changes the
physics engine and controller implementation and uses its separately sourced
Menagerie Panda plant with a first-party pusher.

No ManiSkill robot, mesh, URDF, texture, image, or video asset is redistributed
by this package. The pinned ManiSkill repository contains no upstream NOTICE
file, and push_t.py contains no additional embedded copyright notice.
